#### 8. Exception Handling in Tests — `addNullSkuManualCatch` (line 92)

Manual `try`/`catch`/`fail` pattern instead of JUnit 5's `assertThrows`. If the `fail` call is ever removed, the test silently passes when no exception is thrown.

```java
try {
    catalog.add(null, 1);
    fail("should have thrown");
} catch (Exception ex) {
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

**Refactor** — use `assertThrows`:

```java
@Test
void addNullSkuThrows() {
    IllegalArgumentException ex = assertThrows(
        IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> catalog.add(null, 1));
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Catching broad `Exception` can mask unexpected exception types; fragile if `fail` is removed.

